  "executive_briefing": "The digital asset ecosystem in late August 2026 is navigating a pivotal period marked by imminent regulatory developments and architectural maturity. The pending U.S. Senate cloture vote on September 15 for the Digital Asset Market Clarity Act (H.R. 3633) serves as the primary catalyst for institutional strategy. Meanwhile, institutional capital flows into Bitcoin ETFs and corporate treasuries have entered a consolidation phase following early 2026 net outflows. On the technological front, enterprise preference is diversifying between Ethereum's flexible EVM and Bitcoin's security-first, decidable smart contract execution model (Clarity) to minimize reentrancy risk. Simultaneously, cross-chain DeFi is prioritizing non-custodial direct swap liquidity protocols over legacy wrapped-asset bridges to eliminate centralized trust vectors and slippage across heterogeneous chains.",
